Day 22 – PHP Data Types & Constants
🔹 What I Learned

Data types define how data behaves, and constants protect fixed values.

🔹 Common PHP Data Types
$name = "Chinna";    // String
$age = 21;           // Integer
$price = 99.99;      // Float
$isAdmin = false;    // Boolean

🔹 Arrays
$roles = ["admin", "user", "guest"];

🔹 Constants
define("SITE_NAME", "SecureApp");
define("MAX_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS", 5);

🔹 Security Perspective

Wrong data types can cause logic flaws

Constants help enforce security rules

Never hardcode secrets in code
